From eac1b70b2ae56018869cb41a997b5389cab6e896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:44:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] Move: the battle engine goes from battle.js to
 game/js/logic/battle-engine.js

50 names, same code (move-names.mjs verify: 47 statements moved, nothing else changed): the fighters on the field
(ACTOR_SIDE, fighter, fieldState, liveActors...), effectiveStat, calcDamage, stat stages, status (inflict), useMove,
endTurn, the AI, newBattle, startWild, startTrainer, runTurn, catching odds, items in battle. battle.js keeps the
battle screen (BATTLE UI) and imports them. The file's "BATTLE ENGINE" heading moved with them.

battle-engine.js comes right after saves.js on the game's page, so what it reads from later modules comes through
hooks.js: the battle and the save (activeBattle, setActiveBattle, saveData, uiState), and what it tells the screen
(openBattle and playTurnEvents in battle.js, toast, save, battleWeatherMultiplier). Only BATTLE_RULES, CATCH_RULES
(from RULES) and the actor tables are made at load. The shared renderer still reads fighter and fieldState through
hooks.js (the Studio has no engine).

Checked: lint (no browser globals in the engine), check:modules, format, build, smoke 14/14 (213 s, a loaded machine).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LpFSn4GaodAVzjKW5J3oQR
